title: Project brief, decision register, and verified provider protocol
---
date: 2026-10-17
---
author: Labyricorn
---
summary: Labbonet starts as a written brief, a register of architectural decisions, and a documented, probe-verified provider protocol before any code.
---
tags: architecture, documentation, privacy, local-first
---
source_commit: 6599c2b8b6d1d9a72dc0015b1651947cbdcb1bdd
---
body:

Labbonet began with documents rather than code. The first substantive commit
added the project brief, a decision register, and a protocol note for the Strata
inference server, so that the security and provider choices were written down
and reviewable before an implementation existed.

The decision register gives each architectural question a status. A proposal
becomes an accepted decision only when the project owner explicitly accepts it,
and any later status change is recorded in the register's log rather than made
silently. Fifteen of sixteen decisions were eventually accepted; the routing
decision stays deferred.

The Strata protocol note records what was observed by read-only probes of the
real server instead of what documentation implied. That rule carried through the
project: protocol and capability claims are labeled as verified or unverified,
and ports, authentication, and API formats are not assumed. Later work found
that the served model and context length had already drifted from the note,
which is why the provider adapter records the model a server reports rather
than trusting any document.

The brief also set the commitments that shaped everything after it: loopback by
default, an allowlist of registered endpoints, no executable downloads, and no
firewall or antivirus changes.

[Commit 6599c2b](https://github.com/Labyricorn/Labbonet/commit/6599c2b8b6d1d9a72dc0015b1651947cbdcb1bdd)
